target: internal/record/write.go
verify: go test ./internal/record/ -count=1 -run 'TestEscalationsMustBeAListOfGateAndReason$'
expect: escalations as a list of strings
why:    a list whose elements are not objects — `["security"]`, or a null — is the list-shaped version of the same unreadable or empty escalation. A null decodes, and the report then prints the escalations heading over nothing; a string does not decode at all. Without this guard a string element falls through to the gate check and is refused as naming no gate, which hides that the whole element was the wrong shape.
--- old
		m, ok := e.(map[string]any)
		if !ok {
--- new
		m, ok := e.(map[string]any)
		if false {
